$ mdd -f human sec --help
exit: 0
--- stdout
Extract section content by heading match. When path is a directory, searches across all .md files

Usage: mdd sec [OPTIONS] <PATH> [PATTERNS]...

Arguments:
  <PATH>
          File or directory path

  [PATTERNS]...
          Heading patterns to match (substring, case-insensitive)

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format: human (colored), agent (provenance+signature), json

          Possible values:
          - human: Colored, indented, human-readable
          - agent: Context-efficient with provenance: [file:offset,limit] heading {signature}
          - json:  Structured JSON

      --strict
          Fail on first malformed file instead of skipping with a warning

      --all-files
          Include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE.local.md and README.md in directory scans

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr

